/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A rectangular patch has length L (the resonant dimension) and width W, on a substrate of thickness h and relative permittivity εr.
   - At each of those two edges the field fringes out of the board.
   - The substrate decides size and band.
   - The model treats the patch as a short length of wide microstrip line, open at both ends.
   - W is the width in m for good radiation efficiency; c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s; f is the design frequency in Hz.
   - εeff = (εr + 1)/2 + (εr − 1)/(2√(1 + 12h/W))
   - εeff is the effective permittivity, between 1 and εr because part of the field is in air.
   - ΔL = 0.412h (εeff + 0.3)(W/h + 0.264) / [(εeff − 0.258)(W/h + 0.8)]
   - ΔL is the extra length added by the fringing field at one open end, in m (Hammerstad’s formula).
   - L is the physical patch length in m.
*/
