/* book Worked example: Q: Design a rectangular patch for 2.4 GHz on FR-4 with εr = 4.4 and h = 1.6 mm. Find W, εeff, ΔL and L, and check the resonant frequency.
   1. c/(2f) = 3 × 10⁸/(4.8 × 10⁹) = 0.0625 m.
   2. W = 0.0625 × √(2/5.4) = 0.0625 × 0.6086 = 0.03804 m = 38.04 mm; W/h = 23.77.
   3. 1 + 12h/W = 1 + 12 × 1.6/38.04 = 1.5048, √1.5048 = 1.2267. εeff = 2.7 + 3.4/(2 × 1.2267) = 2.7 + 1.386 = 4.086.
   4. ΔL = 0.412 × 1.6 × (4.386 × 24.04)/(3.828 × 24.57) = 0.6592 × 105.43/94.06 = 0.6592 × 1.1209 = 0.739 mm.
   5. λg/2 = 0.0625/√4.086 = 0.0625/2.0214 = 30.92 mm, so L = 30.92 − 2 × 0.739 = 29.44 mm.
   6. Check: f = c/[2(L + 2ΔL)√εeff] = 3 × 10⁸/(2 × 0.03092 × 2.0214) = 2.400 GHz.
   Answer: W ≈ 38.0 mm, εeff ≈ 4.09, ΔL ≈ 0.74 mm, L ≈ 29.4 mm; the patch resonates at 2.40 GHz in the TM10 mode, about 0.24λ0 long. */
